## How many opaque pixels (to compare "is the person in this image missing an arm").
func _ink(image: Image) -> int:
	var count := 0
	for y in image.get_height():
		for x in image.get_width():
			if image.get_pixel(x, y).a > 0.03:
				count += 1
	return count


## **The portrait must not use the in-game body sprite**: its arms have been stripped (the arms are baked separately per aim direction, see `strip_arms()`),
## and the person in character select would have two empty sleeves (seen in a 2026-09 playtest).
## It now uses the ready-made `portrait.png` in the art pack (cut by `skin_build.py` from the original idle art),
## so it always has a whole arm's worth of pixels more than the stripped body.
